       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as 850 mg three times daily. Single doses are usually 500\u20131,000 mg. The ordered daily total is twice the maximum.\n- **Risk:** This dose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, such as 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO two or three times daily\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is intended, tell me, and I'll need a note on the clinical rationale. I'd also suggest confirming it with pharmacy before I enter it."
