     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and I don't know of any protocol that supports metformin at 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled dose, and a single 1,700 mg dose is also far above normal. If the dose is wrong, the patient could develop lactic acidosis, which is serious and hard to reverse. So I'd rather not enter it on an unverified statement.\n\nHere are some other options:\n- **Enter a dose within range now.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). You can adjust it later if needed.\n- **Go through pharmacy.** If a protocol exists, the pharmacist who reviewed it can enter or co-sign the order through the hospital's override process for out-of-range doses. That also creates the documentation a dose like this needs.\n- **Correct a typo.** If the intended dose was different, such as 850 mg or 1,700 mg total per day, tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
